A||||9||ChadMan||Longitudinally-mounted V8/Eldo tranny
Z||000000||ChadMan||08-16-99||07:39 AM||||I saw it, at the Fiero Festival.  This guy (and I feel like a complete ass because he's a great guy and I can't remember his name!) brought a coupe with a 305 TPI V8 mounted longitudinally in the back.<p>Here's how he did it:  he grafted about two feet into the frame between the firewall and the rear wheels.  Then he did away with the trunk firewall, so he had a nice big engine bay.  He mounted his radiator at the front of the engine bay, then the engine - the transaxle bell-housing butts up against the back of the car.  The engine was covered with a pickup-style tonneau cover, giving the car an El Camino-like appearance, so he named it "El Fiero."<p>People I spoke with either loved it or hated it (those that hated it thought the extra-long rear deck spoiled the lines of the car).  But his craftsmanship was top-notch and I was too impressed with the engineering to be put off by the big rear deck!
